B.Tu=s(["Study in 25-minute focus blocks, then take a 5-minute break. Short sprints beat long, tired sessions.","After each lecture, write three lines from memory. Recalling is stronger than rereading.","In valuation, write the formula first, then put in the figures. Marks are often for the method.","Do past questions early, not only before exams. They show you how lecturers ask.","Teach a topic to a classmate. If you can explain it simply, you understand it.","Sleep is part of studying. A rested brain remembers more than an all-night session.","Link each principle in property law to a real example near you. Stories stick.","Plan tomorrow tonight: pick the two most important tasks and start with the hardest.","Keep a one-page formula sheet for valuation and statistics, and update it every week.","Mix topics when you practise. Switching between them trains you to choose the right method.","Put your phone in another room while you study. Distraction costs more time than you think.","Review your notes within 24 hours of a class. That is when forgetting is fastest.","Thirty focused minutes every day beats a six-hour weekend rush.","Read each question twice and underline what it asks for: the date, the interest, the method."],t.s)
